## 4. The Level — Lightless Caverns

One long, escalating **climb** out of the dark. The opening vignette drops the
pair to the **nadir** (the split happens at the bottom — see `story.md`); from
there the whole level ascends toward a far crack of light (the exit). Acts are
pacing markers in one continuous space. ~**4–5 rooms per act**.
_(puzzle sketches in `level-act1/2/3.md`)_
- **Act 1 — Teach (the bottom):** flip → simultaneity → bodies-as-platforms → threat timing → capstone; ends at the nadir, the climb begins.
- **Act 2 — Test (the climb begins):** linked geometry, separation, rhythmic hazards; first glimpse of light far above.
- **Act 3 — Twist (into the light):** forced gravity-storms, the halves converge, climax at the exit → **merge into one**.

### ✅ Length — long game, hardcore restart, no timer (accepted as-is)
Decision: a **genuinely long** level (long-to-traverse), **full restart on any
death**, **no timer/countdown**. Deliberately punishing — few pairs will finish;
that's the intended identity. The §3 fairness constraints (deterministic,
telegraphed, recoverable, anti-grief) carry the weight of making a long deathless
run *possible*, if brutal.

---

## 5. Characters, World & Goal — see `story.md`

Two halves of one being, split at the bottom of the world and bound to opposite
gravities. **Objective: escape the cave** — climb to the light and become whole
again. Apart in the dark, a half decays into a shadow (the threat). Told
**wordlessly**. Full narrative bible in the companion **`story.md`** artifact.

---

## 6. Multiplayer / Technical — ✅ Local couch

- ✅ Local co-op, two players, one machine, two gamepads.
- **Camera (rec): shared single screen**, framing both surfaces; players can't
  stray off-screen from each other.
- **Engine / tech stack / platform:** owned by the user — out of scope for this doc.

---

## 7. Art & Audio Direction

Tone (**eerie**) + setting (**lightless caverns**).
- **Visual:** silhouette-forward; mirrored tunnel as composition (two figures,
  opposite walls, lethal void between). Deep blacks, cold palette, bioluminescent
  accent. Minimal UI. Flip needs a clear, readable tell.
- **Audio:** sparse cave ambience, drips, distant movement; sound telegraphs
  threats; satisfying *whump* on each flip.
